<title>USA: La Jolla gets U.S. patent for Lupus drug.</title>
<headline>La Jolla gets U.S. patent for Lupus drug.</headline>
<dateline>SAN DIEGO 1996-10-01</dateline>
<text>
<p>La Jolla Pharmaceutical Co said on Tuesday it received a third U.S. composition of matter patent on its lupus drug candidate, LJP 394.</p>
<p>The patent, which expires in 2013, covers compositions of matter and methods of synthesis of a family of lupus compounds based on La Jolla's Tolerance Technology and is the third U.S. patent issued to the company for its LJP 394 lupus Toleragen, La Jolla said.</p>
<p>The company said it planned to start Phase IIb clinical trials for LJP 394 in the &quot;near future.&quot;</p>
<p>--New York Newsdesk, 212-859-1733</p>
